[agent] ## Summary
[agent] I produced the feature table entirely on Databricks (all work ran server-side via the SQL warehouse and Lakebase; nothing computed locally).
[agent] **Offline feature table** — `workspace.mlpab824ae3.features74f1ef`
[agent] - A Unity Catalog feature table with **primary key `row_id`** and **`event_time` declared as the `TIMESERIES`** (event-time) column, Change Data Feed enabled.
[agent] - 700 rows (one per input row, all `row_id` distinct), columns exactly: `row_id, account_id, event_time, amount_usd, is_weekend, amount_7d`.
[agent]   - `amount_usd` = `amount × fx_rate` (joined on currency) — verified e.g. EUR 15.41×1.09 = 16.7969.
[agent]   - `is_weekend` = computed purely from epoch-ms in UTC via `((floor(event_time/86400000)+4) % 7) IN (0,6)` — timezone-independent (Sat/Sun → 1). 483 weekday / 217 weekend.
[agent]   - `amount_7d` = `SUM(amount) OVER (PARTITION BY account_id ORDER BY event_time RANGE BETWEEN 604800000 PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW)` — the inclusive 7-day (604,800,000 ms) window up to and including the row. Verified accumulation within an account.
[agent] **Online / low-latency access** — Online Tables are now deprecated on this workspace ("Creating new online table is not allowed… switch to Synced Tables"), so I used the platform's current real-time path:
[agent] - Created Lakebase database instance **`mlpab824ae3-lakebase`** (CU_1, AVAILABLE).
[agent] - Created **synced database table `workspace.mlpab824ae3.features74f1ef_online`** from the feature table (PK `row_id`, timeseries `event_time`), now in state `SYNCED_TABLE_ONLINE_NO_PENDING_UPDATE`.
[agent] All objects live in the per-run schema `workspace.mlpab824ae3`, and the database instance is prefixed with `mlpab824ae3`, so they're isolated and cleaned up correctly. The offline Delta table and the online synced table give the platform's two distinguished read paths.
